From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: Add a Kconfig symbol for each BCM283x device model

The BCM283x peripheral models are built only when the board symbol
CONFIG_RASPI is set, so a new SoC cannot reuse one of them without
pulling in every Raspberry Pi 1-4 board. Give each model its own
symbol, selected by RASPI, as BCM2835_SPI and BCM2835_I2C already do.

The property device calls into the framebuffer and OTP models, so
BCM2835_PROPERTY selects both; the GPIO models move SD cards between
the SD controllers, so they select SD. The framebuffer helpers are now
selected by BCM2835_FB instead of by the board.

No functional change: RASPI selects every new symbol, so the raspi
machines are built exactly as before.
